      "problem": "Which of the following numbers are divisible by $6?$\n\nI. $11\\,289\\,643$\n\nII. $13\\,298\\,784$\n\nIII. $215\\,153\\,238$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $6$ if it is divisible by both $2$ and $3.$\n\n- The number $11\\,289\\,643$ is not divisible by $2,$ so it is not divisible by $6$ either.\n\n- The number $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n1+3+2+9+8+7+8+4=42\n$$\n\nSo, $13\\,298\\,784$ is divisible by $6.$\n\n- The number $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $2,$ and it is also divisible by $3$ since the sum of its digits is divisible by $3:$\n\n$$\n2+1+5+1+5+3+2+3+8=30\n$$\n\nSo, $215\\,153\\,238$ is divisible by $6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
